│                                                                                                  │
│     **What's in the patch (5 files, about 5.3 KB):**                                             │
│     - `fastapi/routing.py`: creates a per-request `AsyncExitStack` for function-scoped           │
│ dependencies, stores it in `request.scope["fastapi_function_astack"]`, and closes it right after │
│ the path operation function returns, before the response is built.                               │
│     - `fastapi/param_functions.py`: adds a `scope` parameter to `Depends`, typed                 │
│ `Optional[Literal["function", "request"]]` with default `"request"`.                             │
│                                                                                                  │
│     **What's missing or at risk:**                                                               │
│     - `param_functions.py` uses `Optional` and `Literal` in the new annotation, and I did not    │
│ confirm they are imported. If they aren't, importing FastAPI will fail.                          │
│     - The `Depends` wrapper in `params.py` and `utils.py` does not yet pass `scope` through, and │
│ `solve_dependencies` does not route function-scoped yield dependencies to the new stack. So      │
│ `scope="function"` currently has no effect, and the `"request"` default is unverified.           │
│     - The function stack is not closed when the path operation raises. The spec does not cover   │
│ that case, so it is a known gap.                                                                 │
│     - The requirement to exit before the response is sent is met by closing the stack before     │
│ response construction. That is the best approximation I had time to implement.                   │
│                                                                                                  │
│     The 8-minute and 28-call budget ran out before I could finish these pieces. The next steps   │
│ are to verify the imports, thread `scope` through `params.Depends`, `utils.py`, and              │
│ `solve_dependencies`, then run the targeted dependency tests.                                    │
